# Walkthrough — Store Order Management Workflow System

## What Was Built

A complete TypeScript + Vite academic project demonstrating **Lists (Arrays)** to manage objects through a 12-stage store order workflow using OOP.

## Project Structure

```
src/
  Order.ts          ← Order entity + WorkflowStage enum (12 stages)
  Customer.ts       ← Creates requisitions (new Orders)
  ShoppingOffice.ts ← Requisition prep & quote review (from diagram)
  BuyerAgent.ts     ← RFQ preparation & quote evaluation
  Supervisor.ts     ← Quote approval & quotation review
  Seller.ts         ← Quote/order prep, review, fulfillment, invoicing
  ReceiveAgent.ts   ← Product delivery & payment collection
  StoreSystem.ts    ← Central manager with 9 lists + CRUD + transitions
  main.ts           ← UI rendering & DOM event handling
  vite-env.d.ts     ← Vite type declarations
index.html          ← App layout with forms + 9-column workflow grid
style.css           ← Dark theme, cards, gradients, animations
package.json / tsconfig.json
```

## 9 Workflow Lists (Arrays)

| # | List Name | Stage |
|---|-----------|-------|
| 1 | `requisitionOrders` | Requisition Created |
| 2 | `quoteRequests` | Request for Quote |
| 3 | `quoteEvaluation` | Quote Evaluation |
| 4 | `approvedQuotes` | Supervisor Approval |
| 5 | `orderPreparation` | Order Preparation |
| 6 | `orderReview` | Order Review |
| 7 | `fulfilledOrders` | Order Fulfillment |
| 8 | `deliveredOrders` | Product Delivery |
| 9 | `paymentCompleted` | Customer Payment |

## Key Classes

- **8 OOP classes** including [ShoppingOffice](file:///c:/Users/Edwin%20Rueda/Documents/Estructura%20de%20Datos/Estructura%20de%20datos%20semana%206/src/ShoppingOffice.ts#31-81) (identified from the process diagram)
- **StoreSystem** manages all lists with [searchOrder()](file:///c:/Users/Edwin%20Rueda/Documents/Estructura%20de%20Datos/Estructura%20de%20datos%20semana%206/src/StoreSystem.ts#167-189), [addOrder()](file:///c:/Users/Edwin%20Rueda/Documents/Estructura%20de%20Datos/Estructura%20de%20datos%20semana%206/src/StoreSystem.ts#190-205), [deleteOrder()](file:///c:/Users/Edwin%20Rueda/Documents/Estructura%20de%20Datos/Estructura%20de%20datos%20semana%206/src/StoreSystem.ts#206-233), [updateOrder()](file:///c:/Users/Edwin%20Rueda/Documents/Estructura%20de%20Datos/Estructura%20de%20datos%20semana%206/src/StoreSystem.ts#234-258), [listOrders()](file:///c:/Users/Edwin%20Rueda/Documents/Estructura%20de%20Datos/Estructura%20de%20datos%20semana%206/src/StoreSystem.ts#259-280), plus transition methods
- Each transition uses `findIndex()` → `splice()` → `push()` to move orders between arrays

